   "unsent_at": "2026-06-30T23:31:53.950000Z"
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_7b21f5d3",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "contact_7d70e40f0bedb6145566bc4c",
   "text": "oops wrong pic",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:32:02.071000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_e05c8a6f",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "contact_7d70e40f0bedb6145566bc4c",
   "text": "it was the ground lug like you said, this one under the cap bracket",
   "attachments": [
    {
     "name": "au555a-ground-lug.jpg",
     "mime_type": "image/jpeg"
    }
   ],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:33:09.538000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_4f9d3b10",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "ms_user_kofi",
   "text": "That's great to hear, Terrence. Was the nut loose, or had the ground wire come off the lug?",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:39:02.846000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_b812e7c4",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "contact_7d70e40f0bedb6145566bc4c",
   "text": "loose. pulling the old cans let the nut back off, and the new caps are on a little board now so nothing holds that lug tight",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:40:37.129000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_29a6d0f8",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "contact_7d70e40f0bedb6145566bc4c",
   "text": "so ground was going thru the bracket paint. scraped it to bare metal, star washer, cranked it down",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:41:15.774000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_f37c1e95",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "ms_user_kofi",
   "text": "That's the classic one after a recap. A painted joint makes a high-resistance ground, so the ripple current through it shows up as hum. Bare metal and a star washer is the right fix.",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:44:58.309000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_6ad84b2e",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "contact_7d70e40f0bedb6145566bc4c",
   "text": "took it slow on the first power-up like you said, a buddy's variac a little at a time. nothing got warm so i plugged it in straight",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:47:23.660000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_0e5f9c37",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "ms_user_kofi",
   "text": "Good, keep doing that on every first power-up. Next I'd check DC offset at the speaker terminals, then set idle current from the service manual now that it's quiet.",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:53:40.418000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_d4b72a61",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "contact_7d70e40f0bedb6145566bc4c",
   "text": "offset is 8 mV left, 11 right. got the service manual pdf but havent touched bias yet, prob this weekend",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:55:29.092000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_83c1e0b9",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "ms_user_kofi",
   "text": "Those offsets are fine. For bias, give it about 15 minutes to warm up and move the trimmers in small steps.",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-06-30T23:58:49.735000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_5a0f6d24",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "contact_7d70e40f0bedb6145566bc4c",
   "text": "will do. seriously thank you man, i was this close to boxing it back up for good",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-07-01T00:03:31.281000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_c2e93f78",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_5e8a2c71",
   "sender_id": "contact_7d70e40f0bedb6145566bc4c",
   "text": "gonna post an update in the group so the next person with a 555A finds it 👍",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-07-01T00:04:18.906000Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_917b4d0a",
