  {
   "id": "ms_msg_b91d4f27",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_3c9e71a4",
   "sender_id": "ms_user_kofi",
   "text": "Hi Marcus, no trouble at all. Yes, it's available. It was serviced on my bench in September: power supply recapped, new dial lamps, controls and switches cleaned, all functions to spec. Graded Very Good under our written guide, which here means light scuffs on the top cover you can see at arm's length. Faceplate and dial glass are clean.\n- Kofi, Corktown Audio Works",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-10-11T13:42:18.905377Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_5e28a0c3",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_3c9e71a4",
   "sender_id": "contact_624483321982237cde191eea",
   "text": "Sorry, one more basic one. Does it have a phono input? My uncle gave me his old Technics belt-drive and I'd like to run it through this. And what kind of speakers would you pair with it? 👍",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-10-11T16:06:51.228640Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_c47f9b12",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_3c9e71a4",
   "sender_id": "ms_user_kofi",
   "text": "Yes, there's a phono input with a ground post, so the Technics plugs straight in. For speakers, anything rated 8 ohms and around 87 dB or more will be happy on it. At pick-up I can play it through a pair on the bench so you hear it first.",
   "attachments": [],
   "created_at": "2026-10-11T16:31:09.774013Z",
   "unsent_at": null
  },
  {
   "id": "ms_msg_2d6be894",
   "thread_id": "ms_thread_3c9e71a4",
   "sender_id": "contact_624483321982237cde191eea",
